# Frontend — Advanced

Enable when rule level includes `advanced`. Forms/UI/validation **defaults stay on**.

- One UI baseline route owns the visual language; shells inherit it
- Motion budget 2–3 intentional motions; honor `prefers-reduced-motion` (pause Lottie when reduced)
- Performance: **lazy load** routes/chunks (locked); optimize LCP; avoid layout thrash
- i18n-ready copy when Profile lists multiple languages
- If SEO = `on`, wire titles/meta/Schema.org per `seo.mdc`
- Empty / loading / error / 404 states use shared animated defaults (`icons-states.mdc`) — first-class
- Skeleton loaders stay on for primary async regions — do not drop for “speed”
- Do not abandon custom form system or icons-states defaults for “speed”
